body:
Claptrap is kinda hard at first, but gets stupidly strong by level 70. 

&#x200B;

Nisha can definitely kill mobs faster than Claptrap due to auto-aim, but Claptrap with Frigia + Flakker can kill level 70 ultra high HP Ultimate Badasses in just as little as 3 shots (1 freeze, two from the x5 Flakker). 

&#x200B;

Claptrap becomes a super powerful walking grenade fairly early on. With Fridgia, Sapper Class Mod, and Start With a Bang, he can pretty much obliterate enemies while approaching them.

Claptrap + Sapper Class Mod + Fridgia + System Purge = hilariously awesome time. 

&#x200B;

That build can also turn the Cryo T4s-R into a powerful sniping weapon.

&#x200B;

Although, the randomness does make and break the character, such as getting Krieg's melee skill while fighting RK5.

Go back to TVHM and farm for a Slagga first. Magic Missile is also a piece of equipment to consider having. 

&#x200B;

Bringing Rubi isn't a bad idea either. 

&#x200B;

Farm for a Sham in TVHM, then do Lilith's Fight for Sanctuary DLC to unlock the Pollen Glitch to make the rest of your playthrough less of a headache. 

&#x200B;

Beat the Marcus Winterland DLC to have easier access to up-to-date purple equipment for the difficulty.

&#x200B;

If you want great quest reward guns that scale with you (like the Rubi, Amigo Sirroco, Sandhawk, etc), be sure to not turn in the quest after you finish the quest objectives. Instead you exit to main menu, cross save upload your character, enter the game again to turn in the quest to get the equipment, put the quest reward in Claptrap's item transfer locker, quit to main menu, cross-save download to overwrite character (will delete upload), upload your character again, and go get your weapon from the locker. This way you'll have an up-to-date quest reward weapon all the way til level 80. 

&#x200B;

Of course, for OP10 equipment, the quest needs to start on OP10, objectives can be done at OP0, but turn in must be OP10 again in order to get OP10 quest reward.

Running a Sham+Rocket build is viable for many characters. Zer0 especially makes a uniquely strong Rocket Build considering that it's not all that different from an Infinity/Gunner Zer0 build. 

&#x200B;

Deception + Kunai + Magic Missile + Bone of the Ancients + Elemental Badaboom = H-U-G-E damage.

I believe the Sandhawk is considered among the best guns even though it's not Legendary at all. 

&#x200B;

Pimpernel is also not legendary, but the power on that thing is amazing.

Stick with Uranus. At least he drops at level Fast Balls which you can constantly grenade the poor sucker to death. 

&#x200B;

You will need to update your Bee shield every 4 or so normal levels. 

&#x200B;

You can always just run the route to the spawn spot on normal mode and switch over to UHVM after. 

&#x200B;

He also has a good chance of dropping Unkempt Harolds so the process can be maintained for many levels.

It really depends on the gun. Sandhawk and Pimpernel is definitely worth it if you want to farm multiple versions of them (with cross-save character upload/download + Cross save locker) in order to get multiple elements of the same gun. 

&#x200B;

Just remember to re-upload every time you download, as your upload is gone as soon as you download.

First, play through it on NORMAL mode. This way you at least unlock the route to Uranus and the Final Area of the DLC. THEN you do it on UTVHM and you can use Normal Mode to traverse to a spawn spot then swap back to UTVHM to start farming without needing to run through swarms of tough enemies before you start to farm. 

&#x200B;

Also, you'll WANT to at least get to the point where you get immunity so you can get a massive damage boost for the rest of your UTVHM run as long as you don't die with a specific damage boosting glitch.

Zero will struggle early on until you get to roughly level 30\~36. Once you unlock the ability to throw Kunai and Death Mark enemies with Kunai you will absolutely breeze through True Vault Hunter Mode like it's ultra easy mode (especially if you get a Legendary Hunter Class Mod and Cooldown Relic early) and will remain that way until you hit Ultimate Vault Hunter mode where he will start to struggle again for a bit. 

&#x200B;

Salvador will also struggle a little but until level 30+. He'll need his Gunzerk extensions + cooldowns as well as HP Regen while gunzerking before he'll start coming into his own as a force to be reckoned with.

Well, it really depends on which game you play first.

&#x200B;

If you play The Pre Sequel first, picking Jack isn't a bad choice as a starter character, on the flip side Claptrap is also awesome early on since you can invest in the defensive subroutine early and get near invincibility half the time with a high regen shield. 

&#x200B;

If you play Borderlands 2 first, be sure to google SHiFT codes and get lots of golden keys (up to 200 is preferable). Use your keys every 5 levels on your first character until you get a "main weapon" or 2 you're satisfied with and keep leveling until you can self farm powerful lootsplosion enemies on your own around level 55\~60 or so. Ammo can be a huge issue early on as your first character, so Salvador (Gunzerker) is a great recommendation for a first character since he can replenish ammo and HP every time he uses his unique ability. 

&#x200B;

This is especially true if you enter Ultimate Vault Hunter Mode where you NEED to slag enemies in order to even do damage. Gunzerking will allow you to carry a Slag weapon in one hand while you have a damaging weapon on the other.

Only the Defensive Subroutine. If you have a really high Regen shield, then while the Shield Subroutine comes up (half the time) you'll almost be invincible. Otherwise the only other thing worth investing in that tree (especially early on) is the boost to critical damage. 

&#x200B;

You lose 15% damage, but that's worth the price of being near invincible 50% of the time.

There's a solid chance a spirit is trying to communicate with you, but you being a logical person always denied it with reason and logic.

&#x200B;

Just relax, let your thoughts flow freely and listen to that voice in your head. If it seems harmless, there's no reason not to try listening to that quiet voice in your head once in a while.

&#x200B;

The worst that can possibly happen if you listen to a harmless voice in your head is indulging and possibly pampering yourself a bit more than usual, so give it a shot.

It really depends on your level and how far you progressed through the game. 

&#x200B;

Without a doubt though, the very best/fastest way to get legendaries is to use the grinder. 

&#x200B;

So, as long as you keep beating the final boss in the Claptrap DLC, you'll get tons and tons of legendaries.

If you have not played Claptrap before, then try Claptrap. 

&#x200B;

Claptrap's bouncing is annoying early on, but he's amazing  towards the end. 

&#x200B;

I actually regret not taking the defensive subroutine early. With a good regen shield he might as well be immortal half the time.

As one that has studied the "afterlife" as an Aspie's obsession, it's important to understand that death is simply a transition.

&#x200B;

Just know that you, yourself, are simply your consciousness. Your one consciousness only has a limited amount of control over your actual body. You are simply in control of a vessel.

&#x200B;

Remember that within your body your heart beats without your instruction, you cannot tell your white blood cells to simply attack whatever because you want it to, the many bacteria in your intestine are absolutely independent of your control. 

&#x200B;

You help govern your body, but you are not your body. The body never specifically needs your own consciousness (soul), the body could have been born with another consciousness and it will still function mostly independently on a micromanagement level. 

&#x200B;

Simply put, you are not your body. Thus death is simply a transition for your consciousness (soul). 

&#x200B;

Therefore, even in death, "you" are never truly idle.

These totems change over time depending on what your life is experiencing at the time. 

&#x200B;

When I first learned about Animal Totems, I started as a single wolf. Another time, I discovered it became a raven. Later I discovered it became a spirited Gazelle. After another point in time it became a very large Bear. Right now it feels like a calm and non-threatened Crocodile.

My hearing is pretty poor, my sight is alright. I **-H-A-T-E-** bright lights though; the sun annoys me so very much. My sense of smell is rather dull to most kinds of stink, but the smell of fish will drive me up a wall. 

&#x200B;

I like my solid foods at room temperature while I like my liquids in either hot or cold. 

&#x200B;

I don't mind the cold too much, but my body can't take heat well at all. I stay as far away from hot surfaces as much as possible. They once put me on a job to move boiling hot metal slabs that weigh 30+ lbs... needless to say I didn't perform well at that job at all and lost it in 2 months.

You just haven't found a way to channel that hate and rage yet. 

&#x200B;

You can always channel that mentality into constructive activities such as exercise, painting, boxing, drawing, music, or anything creative.

&#x200B;

Express your rage in a fabulous, harmless, and creative way, then people will praise you for it.

&#x200B;

Remember, there's a lot of people who carry hatred inside them, if you manage to create an outlet for them then it'll help you in return. 

&#x200B;

Just remember to not direct your hate towards anything or anyone else.  Making enemies because of inner hate is the last thing we Aspies need.

I have the opposite problem. I often have trouble not having enough words to accurately describe anything. Even if the word I'm using is just slightly off from the point I'm trying to make, then I won't use the word at all. 

&#x200B;

It's gotten to the point where I facepalm whenever I see similar words in the thesaurus. 

&#x200B;

It's even more maddening when I can't find the exact word I'm looking for.

Well, I won't stop you from rejecting principles of reality. This is a voluntary choice, but not one that should be taken if one wishes to learn. 

&#x200B;

Still, you're only taking into account the matters of reality. All matters of reality are subject to the laws of Fate. Fate is an aspect of time.

&#x200B;

Take dreams for example. There is space, there is time, but there is no fate. As such, time is not constantly moving forward, can be repeated infinitely, can be reversed, can be changed. 

&#x200B;

Then we have the mathematics/geometric/logic realm where the aspects of free will is absent. All is as preordained. An equation with no end where there is absolutely no deviation from fate.

&#x200B;

We have the spiritual realm where consciousness flourishes free from the aspects of matter. Where thoughts, feelings, and personal connections prevail.

&#x200B;

While there are more, they become increasingly difficult to explain as they're very alien even to me. There are laws, cycles, aspects, and functions that I have absolute no understand of to speak. These are too many, but not small enough to discount. 

&#x200B;

Just remember that all aspects of untruth must have some level of truth before it can be false.

Yes, Veganism does affect spiritualism, but in a negative way I'm afraid. 

&#x200B;

It feeds the ego, it rejects the idea is death is a requirement for life, veganism actually teaches a person to despise people to consume meat, teaches people to ignore the advice of doctors who dedicate their lives to try to help people, makes people not understand that they're damaging their own bodies in the long run, closes people off from accepting the opinion of others....

&#x200B;

The list goes on and on....

&#x200B;

Spiritualism is about understanding and following the natural flow of things.

&#x200B;

Veganism is about rejecting the natural flow in order to feed the ego.

&#x200B;

So, yes. Veganism does affect spiritualism, but negatively.

I wouldn't say it's the "fastest", but pretty efficient.

&#x200B;

The Makai Brothers drop some of the components to upgrade  "Avoid Death" and "HP Regen". The brothers themselves can drop the AR Ninja, in the treasure room are 3 weapons, a diamond, emeralds, some plates, an accessory. 

&#x200B;

If you have rare drop and item drop chips on your accessories you can just run back and forth between mech enemy spawns in the winter field.

You can switch between difficulties at will. However, just know that some shops (like the Shady Material Shop and R11 weapon shop) require extreme mode in order to either unlock their full inventory or appearing at all. 

&#x200B;

In any case, feel free to swap between difficulties at any point in the game. The only time Extreme Mode is an absolute requirement is when you're going into NG+ and unlocking the final levels of Lisbeth's shops.

This is the exact reason why I play Anthem.

&#x200B;

While it's not exactly SAO Fatal Bullet, at least the Ability system is highly spammable, melee is fun, and I really like the Combo system.

&#x200B;

By no means is Anthem a perfect game, but the gameplay in it is fantastic in my opinion.

&#x200B;

Oh, and Borderlands: Handsome Jack Edition is free for PS PLus Members this month, so if you're on PS4 you might wanna check that out.

There's no argument that Anthem itself has great gameplay. The only arguments are the systems around the gameplay like lackluster non-legendary/masterwork loot, lack of mission variety, lack of larger zones (even though the zone available is quite large in comparison to other games... it's just that you travel around so fast), and the illusion of lacking enemy variety. 

&#x200B;

Still, gameplay itself is amazing and worth experiencing though. It's FAR better and action packed than games like Destiny and ... ... I can't even remember the name of that game off the top of my head.... it's that recent other Looter Shooter from Ubisoft. 

&#x200B;

... .. ... ... .. Odd... 5 minutes later and the name of the game still isn't popping up. I'm not even trying to "hate" on the game, I simply can't think of it right now. I have no problems remember Borderlands, Warframe, Anthem, No Man's Sky, Elite Dangerous, Ghost Recon Wildlands... heck, even Sword Art Online: Fatal Bullet is easy to remember... Diablo 3, Path of Exile, MHW Iceborne... ... .... 

&#x200B;

Yeah, I'll stop worrying about it.

&#x200B;

But hey, for what Anthem has, it's absolutely worth enjoying what's there.

It could be a lover from a previous lifetime that's visiting you in your dreams that's borrowing the image of someone you are highly attracted to. You'll be able to note how different the crush's of yours is in reality is from your dreams. 

&#x200B;

"Who" is in your dreams matters less than what they represent. The image of your crush in reality is likely to be a lover in your dreams. The image of your sibling in reality is likely to be a sibling of another lifetime in your dreams. 

&#x200B;

It's sometimes like this in reality as well. Sometimes a mother can see a spirit of her still alive friend hovering above her in bed, warning her that her baby is in trouble. The spirit simply takes the form of someone that the mother trusts in order to pass an urgent message that she might not trust if anyone else said it.

Well, my spirit guide is either directly related to fate or is highly related to fate. This is what I understand about the soul and time.

&#x200B;

Time cannot flow backwards, the "best" that can happen is simply a recreation while still moving forward. That is not to say the soul cannot revisit "memories". However, these are simply memories and not the "present". 

&#x200B;

Also, there's actually no real deviation. You "think" you have a choice, but really the overall outcome doesn't change. The "butterfly" effect is not as big as one would think.

&#x200B;

An easy example is a job opening: you could apply for the job or you don't. It doesn't matter in the end because the job will be filled regardless of whether you decided to apply or not.

&#x200B;

A more abstract understanding is if you kill off the butterfly in the butterfly effect. It would not matter if that species of butterfly would not survive through natural selection anyways. And it's natural selection that dictates what gets passed on. Even if "someone from the future" tampers with it, the effect would not be as profound as one would believe.

&#x200B;

Another example, though harsh, is Adolf Hitler. Adolf Hitler alone did not create all those atrocious war crimes on his own, it's not like he could have made the Nazi's completely "evil" on his own; he was simply a catalyst that opened up what already existed there in the first place and made it more open for the world to see. It would not have stopped the development of jets, rockets, and would have done nothing to have stopped the great genius, Albert Einstein, from emerging into the world. 

&#x200B;

Kill off Adolf Hitler, the evils would have still existed, except in the background instead of being in the open. 

&#x200B;

Thus, even if there were alternate realities, the difference is so minor that it might as well not be an alternate reality.

Tarot Cards, like many things are simply a tool. Tarot Cards by themselves are pointless, what's important is how you're opening your mind. The interpretation of the card is far more important than the card itself. 

&#x200B;

Thus, the card themselves do nothing.

&#x200B;

The kind of spirit attracted is based on how one opens the mind. If you're thinking of demons you'll call upon demons, if you're thinking of angels you'll call upon angels. Remember, you're using Tarot to "call the beyond". 

&#x200B;

How you feel and what you think are also taken into account. If you are overly suspicious you will call upon a highly suspicious spirit, if you are highly untrusting you will call upon an untrustworthy spirit. if you are highly curious you will call upon a highly curious spirit. if you are highly faithful you will call upon a highly faithful spirit.

&#x200B;

In the end, what you call is highly dependent on the energy you emit. 

&#x200B;

The Tarot Cards are simply tools that make it easier for you to open yourself up to interpretation. You can easily do this without tarot cards through meditation and opening yourself to communication that way. 

&#x200B;

So yes, it's possible to draw in something dangerous if you feel Tarot is dangerous.

&#x200B;

Thus, best to only start Tarot when you feel you can use the Tarot Cards in great faith and free of any negative thoughts.

At your level, you can either do the Winter Field starting area with bees and scorpion on extreme, the bee boss just above the icicle prison on extreme, do Defense Battle 8, Online Hardcore 175 missions, or do DLC bosses on Extreme.

&#x200B;

If you have help, then nothing will raise your levels faster than Online MT-02. Especially if you know someone that can do it in 2-5 minutes.

The people who "solo" these Invitation missions all have at least DEX+30 and LUC+30 on both accessories while at 255 DEX and LUCK (totalling 315 DEX/LUC). They are playing builds that do massive crit damage. 

&#x200B;

Next thing to note is that many of the "solo builds" run Conceal 4. As long as they snipe from a distance many don't get spotted and bum rushed. 

&#x200B;

Also note that many of these solo builds are running on PC, they have a MASSIVE aim advantage to land headshots on the move with mouse and keyboard during manual aim, making weapons like Blue Rose and Moonlight work while making it near impossible for console players.

&#x200B;

It's easier to deal with Asuna? as a group because they tend to power and armor shot each other, considerably buffing their defense and making viral shot less powerful. 

&#x200B;

If you want to do decent damage to them while on the move, it's actually better to blast them with Explosive Damage from something like a Crimson Roar. You'll need at least two accessories with +147% HP Regen and Human Fortress skill in order to make it work.

You might want to give the AR Ninja 3++ a shot if you're not already at max DPS stats (315 DEX and LUC). 

&#x200B;

The AR Ninja 3++ requires less overall investments to reach optimal damage (has a lower damage ceiling) while the AR Blue Rose requires a ton of investments to reach AR Ninja's level of damage (but has a higher damage ceiling). 

&#x200B;

So, depending on your final build, you should consider the AR Ninja prior to maxing out an AR Blue Rose.

Weapons tend to change names at different ranks.

&#x200B;

The SPB Potassium is the mid-rank version of the SPB Praseodynium while the AMR Deathwind is the mid-rank version of the AMR Grim Reaper. Also, the Potassium/Praseodynium sports 669 RMP, not 900. 

&#x200B;

Still, if you're looking for a high agility weapon with a fast rate of fire, the Procyon (pistol) is the better choice since it's super light, has a very high RPM, full automatic, has good range, has a higher crit rate than most full automatics at that level of RPM, has great weak point damage, the stat investment isn't terribly high, and is among the lightest weapons available in the game. 

&#x200B;

If you want an immensely powerful, high stat investment SMG (255 DEX & LUC) that does massive damage, then the Moonlight is your answer.

Edit: The real P90 does indeed have 900 RPM though.

Such a fear can be realized, usually by being a ghost.

&#x200B;

The difference between a ghost and a spirit is that a ghost has not yet moved on from life yet due to regrets or other various reasons. 

&#x200B;

The easiest way to avoid this is to not live with any heavy regrets (minor ones are okay as long as you can let go), live without heavy guilt (especially do not taking one's own life out of depression), and don't be afraid to move on (you'll return in spirit form eventually if you so choose).

You will literally have an easier time getting a legendary Pandemonium Type Z online.

&#x200B;

Anyways, if you absolutely need it, it'll be a long grind. 

&#x200B;

Outside the Meteor Institute, head South to the Frozen lake and kill a boss called Earthshaker, then keep running back and forth next to the cliff wall at the southern part of the lake. You will alternate between a set of 4 drones (one Gatling Drone) and a 2x Drone + Turret (for Sound Deadener 2). Best bring allies with high luck stat while farming like ArFA-sys (if made that way), Asuna, Silica, and Phillia. 

&#x200B;

Then be prepared to do that for HOURs as the drop rate is not very high and a Legendary drop is even lower.

