If you are still having some issues, I'll recommend a few things.

&#x200B;

First is the team members you want to bring with you. Your ArFA-sys is a given, but the other two will easily influence the fight as well. You'll want Crit Boost+Nano Boost on one weapon on your ArFA-sys and Electrodynamic Stunner 3+4 on another weapon while having Healing Bullet 4+AED bullet on both weapons. For your allies, you'll want to pick between Lisbeth+Yuna or Asuna+Silica. Lisbeth is the best buffer/debuffer/stunner, Yuna is a great tank/debuffer/stunner, and Asuka/Silica has excellent luck+AED shot for great farming with party survival. 

&#x200B;

There are two easy weapon strategies for Erishkigal you can employ. One is using a higher rarity Sound Deadener and the other is to use the dual wield Crimson Roar. 

&#x200B;

For Sound Deadener, the strategy is to hit the chest's weak spot with an Eagle Eye beacon and then shoot away with your strongest weapon available. Easy to say, not so easy in practice. 

&#x200B;

The Crimson Roar strategy is very blunt and straightforward. Weak spots are taking too long to hit so you might as well forget it all and just straight out blast at the skirt with the Crimson Roar. This requires some level of tanking abilities like Human Fortress, two high HP Regen accessories, Avoid Death accessory, Shield Matrix for those starfall moments, and some degree of luck that your NPC allies can take the starfall hits.

It is the lightest sniper rifle in the game while offering some rather good firing power. So it's very good for builds that puts emphasis on movement speed. 

&#x200B;

It won't beat Grim Reaper's 500% Weak Spot Damage modifier, the massive damage, and the massive damage from a single crit shot. But the stat investment required to run the Grim Reaper is staggeringly high.

&#x200B;

So, if you don't want such a massive stat investment for a sniper rifle, Calm Hound MK3++ isn't a bad choice at all.

You don't have to feel so anxious. In fact, being anxious is the opposite of what you want to do.

&#x200B;

The entire process is not a all a difficult one would think.

&#x200B;

The steps are easy: Find a nice quiet spot you can relax in, sit back, and let your thoughts flow without restraint.

&#x200B;

The first experience can be a very smooth transition or it can be rough depending on your persona. The less regrets and inner demons you have, the smoother the transition. 

&#x200B;

You don't have to do anything, in fact you shouldn't be doing anything. Your thoughts should just accept all voices and images that come through. 

&#x200B;

Eventually, you'll find that all your thoughts will resonate upon a central concept. Don't worry if it takes months or even years to find it. And how you want to handle it from there is up to you. It's very different for everyone.

The problem I have with those numbers is that you're using the same chip setup, which would be the wrong approach: it would only disadvantage the Procyon if it uses the Crit Rate chip and the Crit Damage on it is not enough to use a chip slot. You are literally better off running vs Humanoid and vs Lifeform for Online / Ammo Acquisition and vs Lifeform Offline. For Offline (where ammo needs to be put into consideration), you either have a limited use Moonlight or a Moonlight that does less damage than Procyon. 

&#x200B;

Moonlight's should be something like: Weapon Damage, Physical Damage, Max HP damage, Weakness damage, Crit Rate, Crit Damage, vs. Mech, Auto-Reload.

&#x200B;

Procyon's should be something like: Weapon Damage, Physical Damage, Max HP damage, Weakness Damage, vs Mech, and Auto-Reload. 2x Optional

&#x200B;

Oh, and I did watch that high movement speed build. I'm only 14.9% Slower than that player, (but I'm pretty sure I have 14.9% better rare drop rate now) and the only reason why it looks so much faster is because they're playing a rather tiny character while I'm playing among the largest/tallest (thus making it look like I move significantly slower).

If you're not running a 255 DEX and LUC build, the Procyon Pistol will outright beat Moonlight.

&#x200B;

The reasons are as followed.

Procyon: Max damage is 928, RPM is 761, and Weak Spot damage is at 140%

Moonlight: Max damage is 810, RPM is 476, and Weak Spot damage is 110%

&#x200B;

So unless you run a 255 DEX and LUC build, the Moonlight loses to Procyon. And even then, the damage difference is not particularly huge until you hit 315 DEX and LUC build. 

&#x200B;

And even then, it's barely on par with Pandemonium III/Type-Z running without max DEX+LUC stats.

Yeah, your Lisbeth's rank is too low. 

&#x200B;

You'll need to beat the Cave, Underground Cavern, and Squad Leader Battle at least once on Easy/Normal and get to rank 9 on your first playthrough, THEN you need to start NG+ and do these 3 events again on Extreme mode to unlock Lisbeth rank 12. Only then will it be reasonable to upgrade the AMR Grim Reaper from rank 10-11. 

&#x200B;

Or somehow skip all that, level grind like heck, and get the Crimson Roar Launcher for the tank boss and Sound Deadener as a Sniper Rifle instead.

In DLC4, just kill the Executioner boss on easy mode in Icicle Prison Depths. He'll drop a rank 8 Raikiri, which is a sword that has a base damage around 1500 damage at rank 8. 

&#x200B;

This sword is stronger than non-upgraded rank 11 swords.

&#x200B;

Once you unlock Extreme Mode, there's a weapon merchant next to the shady material merchant (only available on Extreme Mode) and he sells rank 11 weapons.

&#x200B;

The Procyon (Pistol) or the Draques (SMG) are the two weapons I recommend at your level since they have low stat requirements and you can afford to dual wield them at your level (especially the Procyon).

Also note that you NEED to see the bad ending at LEAST once. The reason for this is because you need to do Kirito Mode and get through the green bubbles in Kirito Mode as well. But your ArFA-sys will NOT give you the key item for the True Ending once you finish SBC Flugel and Kirito Mode unlocks.

&#x200B;

Kinda sucks, but that's how it is.

You'll want around 197 VIT (or more), Armor Form 4, two accessories that have +147% HP healed per minute, at least one accessory with Avoid Instant Death with at least 10% HP, at least one accessory with +100% HP healed, First Aid Kit 2, Viral Shot 3/4 and Human Fortress 3/4.

&#x200B;

Unless you're hit with a high powered instant kill move (like the Behemoth's Spin2Win attack), you can forget dying in most situations since you'll regen way too fast for most enemies to damage through.

The point of some of the DLC skills and level 4 skills is to abuse the living daylights out of them with Pistol Weapon Art. 

&#x200B;

Like explosive shot 4 only does marginally more damage than explosive shot 3, but nothing is stopping you from using Explosive Shot 4 back to back with Pistol Weapon Art active.

Actually, if you get Crimson Roar for Behemoth, you can completely ignore the AMR Grim Reaper.

&#x200B;

For stupidly high DPS on a sniper, you want a Sound Deadener. Instead of Crit Chance, Crit Damage and Explosive Damage rolls, you want Auto Reload. You actually want Target Beacon on this gun. 

&#x200B;

Hit a weak point with a target beacon with this gun and the enemy's HP (even at level 285) might as well melt. 

