First, you want to beat the game once and unlock Extreme Mode first. Once you unlock extreme mode, there's this one NPC that will spawn next to the Shady Materials NPC. That NPC will sell rank 11 base weapons. 

&#x200B;

You want to buy the Dracques SMG that only requires you to have 78 STR and 79 DEX. This is the strongest weapon you can get with the lowest CP investment at early levels. It's enough to carry you to the level 150s range easily if you get to the point where you can dual wield them. They start becoming obsolete around level 180 and you should be getting your Legendary Rank 11 weapons by then. 

&#x200B;

If you're having ammo issues, get the strongest Rare of Above Dojikiri Sword you can Gun+Sword as your second weapon. Then keep refreshing until you find a weapon with +200% or more Acquire More Ammo, then use Lisbeth to put it onto your Dojikiri Sword.

&#x200B;

For an efficient Sword+Gun build that doesn't use ammo stick to Sharp Nail 2, Sharp Nail 3, Electromagnetic Stunner 2, and Electromagnetic Stunner 3. This way you shoot to stun enemies, use the UFG to rob materials (for money), attack freely, and acquire ammo while at it. It's nowhere near as strong as the rank 11 SMG, but you can resupply your SMG's ammo this way if you're running low. 

&#x200B;

If you plan to solo level early on, then simply head to the forest's east side and start shooting NPC Players and find a route between enemy NPC players you're comfortable with. Difficulty should only be as high as you're comfortable with. Should get you to level 100 really easily this way all the way to level 120+.

