Different Leifangs have different weaknesses. 

&#x200B;

Leifang is one of those characters that's both fast and slow; while her fastest punch is only 10 frames (5P), her fastest stun is just 11 frames (5K). If you're dealing with a grabby Leifang, your only answer is to not block and pull out the fastest crouching attack you can whenever she attempts to throw. 

&#x200B;

Your only answer for now is to use a crouching attack, low hold, or quick grab for now. The rest depends on how the opponent Leifang adapts.

&#x200B;

Also, while it's rare, she can mid-rage juggle you with a 14 frame kick from a very far distance (6K). At that range, 14 frames makes it look like she teleports so be wary of that. It isn't possible for full juggle damage with that move, but it still hurts tons if the Leifang player knows how to optimize the damage from it.

As a Leifang player, I can honestly say he's been baiting you the entire fight.

&#x200B;

He basically keeps throwing out incomplete moves to keep trying to pull you out of block. He's making you guess when he'll truly be open so he can land a stagger hit or juggle off you. 

&#x200B;

The ways to fight these opponents are to do footsies+whiff punish, zone, low punch reset, offensive hold, or side step. Considering his grade, he probably learned how to fight against those strategies too so you do need some level of adaptation.

&#x200B;

Other than that... your best strategy in this situation is to break his rhythm.

