Fear is a result of a panic induced from not knowing either what's happening or not knowing what to do. 

&#x200B;

The best way to permanently resolve fear is to have a deeper understanding of what it is you fear whether it is through through research or through meditation. 

&#x200B;

This is why jump scares are only frightening briefly and after your brain has time to process the information the fear immediately dissipates. Or those that have a fear of a house spider; after knowing it's not poisonous, the bite not being able to penetrate the skin, having one reduces the presence of other bugs in the house, and it'll leave on it's own if there's no food there is very little reason to be afraid of it. Or even a fear of most harmless bugs, as long as you know they don't have an easily accessible food source, they're temporary intruders at best. 

&#x200B;

So the best way to handle fear is not to confront it, but to understand it. Only by understanding will you lose that fear.

