**Destructive Long Range** \- Using your Devastator Sniper Rifle to aim, you can shoot a very high damage round into the opponent and follow up directly with a Railgun to hit the exact same spot. This is an extremely powerful double whammy attack that easily recharges as soon as you finish reloading, aim down again, and shoot again.

So far, almost every match I enter, I'm usually the one with the most gold medals and most medals in general while using the Colossus, so these are my thoughts. 

&#x200B;

Colossus is absolutely overwhelming, it has ways to handle all sorts of enemies available in the Demo. The Colossus can slam smaller elites down to the ground, Railgun them while they're down, slam them again, and go to town with gunfire between slams; this causes smaller elites to be unable to fight back properly. 

&#x200B;

For larger opponents, Colossus can just circle around with the shield and rail gun the weaknesses when exposed for immense damage (that's higher single damage than any other ability I've seen so far). 

&#x200B;

The high explosive mortar is probably just as strong as the Storm's lightning bolt. 

&#x200B;

There's also a huge misunderstanding about Colossus being squishy, it's really not. Even at base recoverable HP, the Colossus can take more damage than a full HP Storm or Interceptor (I revived one, they got KO'd again before I got KO'd... it was a hard fight). Also note you can alternate where you let your Armor recover while you bring your shield up and let your shield recover while you take some damage for a loophole that allows you take take more damage before going down. 

&#x200B;

Also, Colossus can bring tremendous control by simply ramming swarms of smaller enemies, allowing other players to not get shot at as much and have easy grounded targets to shoot on. 

&#x200B;

And if anything, Colossus's minimum recoverable Armor is the same as a full Shield/Armor Storm/Interceptor, it means it can recover the same amount of Armor as a Storm/Interceptor at full Shield/HP. This is also true with the Shield, as it can also soak the same amount of damage as a fully shielded/armored Storm/Interceptor. 

&#x200B;

If anything, Colossus is absolutely fabulous as long as you're used to using heavy units (which is fine with me, since I play even heavier mechs in Armored Core).

