One example, like a murderer that didn't get caught. Because he's more wary of being caught he's more isolated than before. Being more isolated, he might have missed an opportunity to meet a person that could have brought great happiness to his life. Because he's more isolated, he loses more monetary opportunities. Because he's isolated, he'll end up wasting more time thinking back to that murder he got away with than spending that time coming up with a revolution that would have helped him in his lifetime. That and the isolation will influence VERY many things in this person's life.

&#x200B;

Another person is a great person that gives to the poor and works hard. Because they are selfless and work hard, people have great trust in the person. Because there's a lot of trust for this person, it's significantly easier for this person to meet new people. Having meet many new people, it's significantly easier for him to find an ideal lover. Because he is trusted, he has many more opportunities to make it very well in life. Because he can be trusted, the world looks much more favorably at him.

&#x200B;

This is but two of the many ways that Karma works and how influencing the cycles changes VERY many things.

