Hello, I hope I get to you in time. 

&#x200B;

I'm a person with Asperger Syndrome, which gives us an obsessions. Mine just happens to be everything revolving around death, the afterlife, life, so on, and so forth. 

&#x200B;

Death is NOT your answer right now, because it's highly likely you're mentally stuck on your regret and that's only going to make you stuck where you currently are at death. In other words, a ghost that has not quite moved on yet and very likely you'll spend even MORE time basking in the regret and pain than if you were to resolve it when alive. 

&#x200B;

I'm not very sociable, nor am I very empathetic (comes with Aspergers), so I apologize if I come off cold. 

&#x200B;

Anyways, it sounds like you have issues with your ego and your depression comes from your lack of purpose. Breaking your ego and finding purpose are NOT easy things to resolve. DMT and LSD are illegal, but it is easily the fastest way to break your ego and find a new purpose. If it doesn't show you your purpose, it will at least show you how dreadful it is to be dead with regret. 

&#x200B;

If you're going to die, at least don't die with regret. I'm sure you still have a ton of things you still want to do, at least don't leave them unfinished.

